| N. Iizuka, S. Lin, *Symmetry-resolved genuine multi-entropy: Haar random and graph states*, arXiv:2511.00905v2, §III.2.1, Eqs. (61)–(69), and Appendix B | `literature-attested`: for a graph state with three parties $A,B,C$, Eq. (64), derived in Appendix B from the stabilizer-subgroup count of Bravyi et al. (Eq. (62)), gives the number of extractable GHZ states as $p=\operatorname{rank}_{\mathbb F_2}\Gamma_{A:BC}+\operatorname{rank}_{\mathbb F_2}\Gamma_{B:AC}+\operatorname{rank}_{\mathbb F_2}\Gamma_{C:AB}-\operatorname{rank}_{\mathbb F_2}\tilde\Gamma$, where $\tilde\Gamma$ is $\Gamma$ with its diagonal blocks removed; in the notation of Convention 2.5 this is $p=\tfrac12\big(r(A|BC)+r(B|AC)+r(C|AB)\big)-r(A|B|C)$. Combined with GHZ extraction and the GHZ and Bell-pair values of $S_n^{(3)}$, this gives the masked-rank form of the case $\mathtt q=3$ of Corollary 4.2; the source itself states the resulting entropy only for the genuine multi-entropy at $n=3$ (Eq. (66)). For four parties it conjectures, from numerics at $n=2$, a rank expression for the genuine multi-entropy (Eqs. (67)–(69)); no case $n\ge3$ with $\mathtt q\ge4$ is treated. 